<h3>WC Module Help Page</h3>

<h4>TLD Group general principles regarding the handling of Warranty Claims:</h4>

<p>Unless otherwise agreed upon previously, the liability of manufacturing companies shall 
be limited to the general terms and conditions of the warranty of TLD.</p>

<ul>
  <li>In the case of minor repairs covered by the warranty, manufacturing companies shall 
  pay for parts, and all related expenses (freight, duties...)
    <ul>
      <li>Sales entities shall pay for labour,</li>
      <li>The companies&#8217; travel and accommodations expenses of employees shall be borne 
      by manufacturing companies.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>Major repairs required as a result of manufacturing defects, compulsory service bulletin,
  or due to a failure to comply with customer specifications shall be carried out either by the 
  manufacturing companies themselves or by sales entities at the expense of the manufacturing.</li>
  <li>Sales entities shall be responsible for overseeing repairs under warranty</li>
</ul>

<h4>WARRANTY CLAIM MANAGEMENT :</h4>

<p>The Customer Warranty Claims (WC) within TLD are exclusively managed through our WEB 
interface Service module.<br><br>
After any WC has been originated by a Sales entity or by the customer itself, its status 
is automatically set to PENDING and has to be turned to either ACCEPTED, REJECTED, CONDITIONAL 
or SALES CONCESSION.</p>

<p>The TLD spirit is to manage the customer warranty issue first, without delay, and then to 
manage the warranty cost issues in a second step.</p>

<p>For this purpose, Warranty Part shipping, under Sales entities&#8217; Responsibility, and WC 
acceptance are not linked.</p>

<p>Whenever a WC is initiated by a SSO, has to organize the part shipping through its Parts 
Organization or with the help of other TLD parts hubs.</p>

<p>The WC should therefore be emailed to the relevant Parts Hub that will ship the part and 
record immediately the Shipping tracking information as soon as the part has been shipped.</p>

<p><u>The factory product support Manager (PSM) must however be very diligent and should not keep 
any PENDING status WC for more than 2 working days.</u> Each factory COO&#8217;s should check on 
a regular basis that this rule is well enforced.</p>

<p>Whatever the Sales entity may decide to do with its customer, the factory PSM alone is 
entitled to ACCEPT, REJECT or consider as CONDITIONAL a WC.</p>

<p>On its side, the Sales entity is entitled, at its own cost, to turn the status of a REJECTED 
WC to SALES CONCESSION.</p>

<p>Only ACCEPTED Warranty Claims related expenses can be invoiced by the Sales entities to any factory.</p>

<p><u>The use of CONDITIONAL Warranty Claim must be used on an exceptional basis by the PSM,</u> 
and only in the following cases:</p>

<ul>
  <li>It is absolutely critical for the factory to get the failed part back for investigation 
  purpose (internal one or vendor one)</li>
  <li>The cost of the part is such that it is necessary to have the part back for repair or 
  reimbursement by the vendor</li>
  <li>The PSM cannot conclude about the responsibility or not of the factory without more detailed 
  information.</li>
</ul>

<p>In no case should the factory make use of this CONDITIONAL status to avoid making a prompt 
and thorough investigation regarding the responsibility of the WC, which only will determine 
the party responsible for bearing the related costs.</p>

<p>It is important to note that PSM can request part return even if the WC status is ACCEPTED.</p>

<p>When a WC has been declared CONDITIONAL, it becomes the responsibility of the Sales Entity 
to either immediately challenge this status, in case it would be unreasonable, or to provide 
back the requested part or information in a 2 months timeframe.</p>
  
<p>After these 2 months, in absence of proper feedback from the Sales entity, the WC status is 
automatically changed to REJECTED with email warning to the WC originator and to the PSM.</p>

<p>In this case, the factory is entitled to invoice to the Sales entity all direct costs 
related to this WC incurred by the factory. As soon as the requested data or parts of a 
CONDITIONAL WC have been provided to the factory and investigation done, it is the PSM 
responsibility to promptly adjust the WC status to either ACCEPTED or REJECTED.</p>